\par\par \b \uc2  Cbank  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  seen restraining S.Africa rand. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Luke Baker \par \uc2 593 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 Dezember 1999\par 13:39\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  JOHANNESBURG, Dec 3 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 South Africa\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is expected to hold steady in coming weeks, economists say, but lurking \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  will stop it strengthening as much as it could. \par \par \uc2  Over the past six months, the rand has held comfortably to a band between 6.00 and 6.20 to the dollar, with only brief spikes out of the range. Any strengthening through six has quickly been followed by a move back towards 6.10. \par \par \uc2  In its quarterly economic bulletin, released on Thursday, the Reserve Bank revealed one major reason for the pattern. \par \par \uc2  "The appreciation in the weighted effective value of the rand could have gone further...had it not been for the Reserve Bank's steady purchases of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," the December edition of the bulletin said. Earlier in the day, more information emerged on how much foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been buying. \par \par \uc2  Releasing November reserves data, the Bank said its net open \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  position (NOFP) - its uncovered exposure to fluctuations in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market - declined by $900 million on the month to $14 billion. \par \par \uc2  The numbers were encouraging, and came on the back of a healthy decline in the NOFP (and forward book) in recent months, from $18.3 billion in June this year. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  HOLDS BACK RAND \par \par \uc2  While economists are pleased with the reduction in a liability that makes foreign investors wary and has negative implications for interest rates, it is also holding up the rand. \par \par \uc2  "A base has been formed under the rand, it should be stronger - somewhere closer to 5.80 than 6.15," said Colen Garrow, economist at ABN-Amro in Johannesburg. \par \par \uc2  "But while the rand may not have reached its full potential, the forward book has come down a lot and that's encouraging from several points of view. (Reserve Bank Governor) Tito Mboweni is hell bent on getting the forward book down and he's doing it." \par \par \uc2  Garrow reckons the Bank will continue siphoning dollars out of the market as long as the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  holds between six and 6.25 and for as long as capital inflows to local securities give the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  fundamental support. \par \par \uc2  "As foreigners show interest in the equity market and, to a lesser extent, the bond market, the Bank will take dollars out...we're likely to see the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  around 6.10 in the run up to the budget (in February) rather than 5.90 or below." \par \par \uc2  Some \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  traders are concerned the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's unspecified \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  floor could prompt speculators, who had a bash at the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  last year, to have another go. \par \par \uc2  But most think the Bank's policy will just prevent the rand from moving too close to six to the dollar and that foreign buying of local assets will prevent weakness on the other side. \par \par \uc2  "They're just taking dollars out very calmly, in a very orderly way. The rand is basically rangebound and steady," said one senior trader. \par \par \uc2  With the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  seen stable, and bonds and equities expected to get a boost from fresh capital flows after the millennium, the risk on the horizon may come with the budget. \par \par \uc2  Economists say that if Finance Minister Trevor Manuel decides to loosen exchange controls further, as everyone is clamouring for him to do, there would likely be a period of rand weakness as \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  leaves the country. \par \par \uc2  ((Johannesburg newsroom, +27 11 775 3131, fax +27 11 775 3132, email newsroom@reuters.co.za)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010908dvc308q19\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
