\par\par \b \uc2  S.Africa cbank says no comment on  \highlight22\uc2 fx intervention \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2 305 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Juni 1999\par 18:11\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  JOHANNESBURG, June 22 (Reuters) - The Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 South Africa\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Tuesday declined to comment on market speculation it had taken advantage of the rampant rand to purchase dollars and unwind its heavy exposure in the forward \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. \par \par \uc2  Bertus van Zyl, general manager of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading, told Reuters the Bank's policy of permitting two-way volatility in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  remained intact. \par \par \uc2  This, he said, allowed it to buy small amounts of either rand or dollars from time to time, depending on the circumstances. But he declined to be drawn on specifics. \par \par \uc2  Analysts reckon the bank should sell rand for dollars in order to trim its hefty oversold forward dollar position, which stood at $22.2 billion rand at the end of May. \par \par \uc2  They also say the rand's resurgence - it has jumped to its strongest levels since early February in celebration of the country's peaceful June 2 election - is damaging the country's fragile exports and that the Bank would prefer to see it weaken. \par \par \uc2  South African export earnings have been pressured by the slump in bullion prices to a fresh 20-year low of $258 per ounce and would benefit from a weaker rand, which would make goods made here cheaper in foreign markets. \par \par \uc2  The rand has been boosted by dollar selling after traders said offshore hedge funds cut the long-dollar positions they had established ahead of the elections in anticipation of rand weakness. \par \par \uc2  With such a strong inflow of the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  into the market, dealers say it would be natural for the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to take advantage by soaking up the extra liquidity. \par \par \uc2  ((Johannesburg newsroom, +27-11-775-3131, \par \par \uc2  fax: +27-11-775-3132, e-mail: newsroom@reuters.co.za)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010907dv6m05ybn\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
