\par\par \b \uc2  Medium term prospects bearish for rand - Warburg. \b0\par\par\uc2 336 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 November 1998\par 11:18\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, Nov 16 (Reuters) - The medium term prospects for the rand are poor, although the short term outlook, buyoed by further interest rate cuts among G7 countries, is more favourable, analysts at Warburg Dillon Read said. \par \par \uc2  "With the rand now at levels reflecting overvaluation ... and with the possibility of the economy only running sustained current account surpluses in the next five years at the earliest, the rand remains vulnerable to further bouts of turbulence," analyst Mansoor Mohi-uddin wrote in a client note published on Friday. \par \par \uc2  Warburg said the rand would fall to 7.00 per dollar by the end of 1999, after rising from a low of 6.84 to the dollar in late August to a recent 3-1/2 month high of 5.48 as hedge funds and proprietary desks have closed out long dollar positions. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 South Africa\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has held back from \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to cap the rand's gains, allowing it to strengthen. \par \par \uc2  "In the short term, we believe that the absence of leveraged players/proprietary desks and the further prospect of G7 interest rate cuts will provide further near term support for the rand," Warburg said. \par \par \uc2  But looking further ahead: \par \par \uc2  "While national elections in 1999 and the appointment of a new governor to the SARB are less likely to provoke \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  turbulence...the 'reliquification' of global markets by U.S. interest rate cuts will enable leveraged players in the medium term to target more liquid emerging market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  once again." \par \par \uc2  Warburg said the outlook for South African government debt was likely to be similar. \par \par \uc2  While bond yields may fall over the following three months: "over a one-year time horizon, bouts of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  turbulence are likely to reflect in yields periodically spiking higher again, and pre-crisis highs in the bond market, when yields fell to 12.4 percent, look out of reach." \par \par \uc2  ((Carolyn Cohn, London newsroom +44 171 542 6320, uk.\b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2 .news@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010926dubg04hgz\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
