\par\par \b \uc2  PRESS DIGEST - South Africa - Sept 25. \b0\par\par\uc2 538 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 September 1998\par 10:09\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  JOHANNESBURG, Sept 25 (Reuters) - These are the leading stories in the South African press on Friday. \par \par \uc2  Reuters has not verified these stories and does not vouch for their accuracy. \par \par \uc2  - - - - \par \par \uc2  BUSINESS DAY \par \par \uc2  - The rand firmed against the dollar last night, accompanied by a firmer gold price, as Japanese and Hong Kong stock prices surged on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  - Voicing faith in Deputy President Thabo Mbeki's "assertive leadership" and government's commitment to prudent fiscal and monetary policy, US credit rating agency Duff & Phelps said it saw no reason to downgrade South Africa's long-term foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and rand debt from BBB-and A-respectively, and declared the outlook "stable". \par \par \uc2  - The Federal Reserve Bank in New York has co-ordinated a 3.5 billion dollar baleout of one of the largest U.S. hedge funds, following fears that a collapse could worsen the contagion in financial markets. \par \par \uc2  - The Financial and Fiscal Commission, the body charged with advising government on provincial finances, is worried that government is stalling the devolution of taxation powers to the provinces. \par \par \uc2  - The Food and Allied Workers' Union (Fawu), racked by claims of financial irregularities, is unable to pay staff salaries this month. \par \par \uc2  - - - - \par \par \uc2  BUSINESS REPORT \par \par \uc2  - South Africa's vehicle manufacturers were owed an estimated 1.5 billion rand by the government for taxes paid in lieu of export benefits that should have been tax free, Roger Pitot, a consultant to the National Association of Automobile Manufacturers of South Africa (Naamsa), said on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  - The Russian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  called for tough price controls on Thursday, warning that without prompt action inflation could explode to between 400 percent and 450 percent by the end of the year. \par \par \uc2  - Eskom, the state electricity utility, was expected to pump 40 million rand to 60 million rand annually into Esmed, its medical aid scheme, a top Eskom source said on Thursday. Esmed was not expected to break even in the next four years. \par \par \uc2  - A bitter row between the Council for Nuclear Safety (CNS) and the department of minerals and energy over radiation safety in mines had to do with money rather than safety, senior government and industry sources said this week. \par \par \uc2  - - - - \par \par \uc2  THE STAR \par \par \uc2  - As an uneasy calm returned to a devastated Maseru on Thursday after three days of looting and mayhem, President Nelson Mandela angrily described criticism of \b \highlight22\uc2 South Africa\b0 \highlight\uc2 's military \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Lesotho as "ignorance". \par \par \uc2  - Cultural diversity was the theme of Thursday's Heritage Day festivities as South Africans celebrated with prayer, dance and song. \par \par \uc2  - It's get-away weather for those who want to get out and about this weekend, with the Weather Bureau predicting that most of Gauteng will be fine but partly cloudy. \par \par \uc2  - - - - \par \par \uc2  THE CITIZEN \par \par \uc2  - The voluntary removal from Fourways High School, Johannesburg of four girls accused of involvement in tuckshop thefts to totalling 48,000 rand was "tantamount to expulsion", governing body chairman Mike Hogan said on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  - A planned rolling protest by organised agriculture against farm killings has drawn support from a wide spectrum of other organisations and could turn into a mass demonstration against crime and the government's handling of it. \par \par \uc2  ((Johannesburg newsroom, +27 11 482-1003 \par \par \uc2  newsroom@reuters.co.za)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020021108du9p01xa6\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
