\par\par \b \uc2  FOCUS-SAfrica rand plunges as attack renewed. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Alister Bull \par \uc2 543 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 Juni 1998\par 10:35\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  JOHANNESBURG, June 29 (Reuters) - South Africa's rand plunged on Monday as speculators renewed their month-long assault against the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  that has inflicted crushing losses against the dollar and pound. \par \par \uc2  The rand vaulted 6.00 against the dollar in a headlong slide to a fresh all-time low of 6.150. \par \par \uc2  This represents a 13 percent loss on Thursday morning's 5.420 against the dollar and 21 percent since May 22 when a widening emerging market crisis provoked the first blatant speculative attack. \par \par \uc2  Economists reckon the heavy decline in the rand's value is not justified by its macroeconomic fundamentals - which might be weak in some areas like the balance of payments and growth but are generally regarded as solid. \par \par \uc2  But this has cut little ice with hedge-fund sellers, who shrugged off reported \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on behalf of the Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 South Africa\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Federal Reserve and Bank of England late on Friday and on Monday were swift to take up cudgels again. \par \par \uc2  "This is a very unhappy situation. The rand's movement is not justified by fundamentals, but the global environment is not favourable," said economist Peter Worthington at JP Morgan. \par \par \uc2  Dealers reported unprecedented \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  aid from Britain and the United States on Friday afternoon, but this failed to halt the headlong slide. There has been no official comment on reports of a concerted round of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The Reserve Bank has limited options at its disposal to defend the rand. It is expected to lift official interest rates at its daily money market repo auction at 1000 GMT to back over 20 percent, from 18.31 percent on Friday. \par \par \uc2  But analysts fear a such a step would penalise the fragile economy and have little chance of scaring off speculators. \par \par \uc2  They were equally sceptical that official \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  could stem the tide running against the rand. \par \par \uc2  The country's gross official reserves stood at just 32.9 billion rand at the end of May - nowhere near enough to stave of market selling that time and again has demonstrated that it can master almost any amount of official support. \par \par \uc2  June reserves will be posted on Tuesday and a Reuters survey expected them to decline to around 31 billion rand. \par \par \uc2  No one was prepared to stick their neck out over how much the Bank's crucial uncovered position on its forward \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  book would have changed over the month after it soared unexpectedly to $17.9 billion at end-May from $12.8 billion in April. \par \par \uc2  South Africa has now endured over a month of abuse at the hands of international \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  speculators and JP Morgan's Worthington said it was extremely hard to judge when this would be exhausted. \par \par \uc2  But he predicted a sharp recovery in rand values when the selling stopped - mirroring the boost it gained when its last trail by \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer in 1996 ended. \par \par \uc2  Then, a collapse to 4.50 against the dollar from 3.60 on an attack sparked by fears over the health of President Nelson Mandela saw prices bounce back to 4.30 once the attack faded. ((Johannesburg newsroom, 27-11-482-1003 newsroom@reuters.co.za)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du6t01uwp\par }\page {\pa