\par\par \b \uc2  South African Rand Tumbles Despite Reported Joint  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 1,129 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 Juni 1998\par 20:12\par \uc2  Dow Jones Online News \par \uc2 DJON\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  JOHANNESBURG, \b \highlight22\uc2 South Africa\b0 \highlight\uc2  -(Dow Jones)- In what amounted to a new Black Friday for the South African \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, the rand plunged about 6% against the dollar - its biggest single-day drop - and prompted the South African Reserve Bank to reportedly seek assistance from the Federal Reserve and the Bank of England. \par \par \uc2  The South African government, meanwhile, is facing growing pressure to engineer a new fiscal strategy to stabilize the beleaguered \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and to stave off a repeat of 1996, when the rand plunged 22% amid fears about the fledgling democracy's economic credentials. \par \par \uc2  The rand has tumbled more than 15% against the dollar this year, as the Asian economic crisis hobbled the fragile South African economy. Analysts said the rand was an easy target for speculators after the government eased its key repurchase, or repo, rate earlier in the week. Dwindling foreign reserve levels also left the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  vulnerable. \par \par \uc2  The country had sharply lifted interest rates recently to bolster its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and keep investment within the country. In the past few days, though, it nudged the repo rate below its highest levels, which helped spark Friday's rand selling. \par \par \uc2  The reported \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  temporarily pushed the dollar down to around 5.7000 rand from just under 5.8000 rand. But the rand's strength quickly faltered, as the dollar's downward momentum was halted within half an hour of the first reports of Fed \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The dollar then made a sharp recovery, soaring through 5.8000 rand and settling at 5.8950 rand in Johannesburg, up from 5.5875 Thursday. In New York trading, the dollar soared to a record high at 5.9655 rand from 5.5875 rand a day earlier. \par \par \uc2  None of the three three central banks would comment on their reported roles Friday in what appears to have been the first instance of concerted \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  for the South African \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . But traders in in London, New York and Johannesburg were adamant that the U.S. and British central banks had been in the market. \par \par \uc2  "I suspect that they (the Fed and the Bank of England) are doing it with South Africa's money, but the problem is South Africa doesn't have a lot of reserves," said Mark Chandler at Deutsche Bank Securities. \par \par \uc2  Chris Stals, head of the South African \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , said he had no knowledge of whether the Federal Reserve and Bank of England bought rand for dollars on South Africa's behalf Friday. But he said it "isn't unusual" for other central banks to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  on behalf of the South African Reserve Bank should \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  weakness occur outside the Johannesburg market's hours. \par \par \uc2  The rand has been softening against the dollar on and off for several years, as South Africa continues to open up its once-insular economy to international competition following the dismantling of apartheid. \par \par \uc2  Traders had expected the rand to continue to fall against the dollar, but the declines in recent weeks have pushed the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  well past forecasts, and South Africa has largely depleted its reserves to defend the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The weaker rand is of some benefit to the country. Although it makes imports more expensive for South African buyers, and raises fears of capital flight, the decline makes South African products less expensive for foreign buyers. Many economists in South Africa have felt the rand must depreciate further if South African exports are to compete on global markets. Meanwhile, many Asian and African \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  have fallen much more sharply than the rand. \par \par \uc2  Having depleted its scant holdings of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  heavily in May and early June to defend the rand - South Africa spent $6.60 billion to buy the rand in May before changing tack in mid-June by raising rates - most market participants believe the Reserve Bank really has no choice but to send rates sharply higher once again to defend the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  On Friday, the bank started to do just that. The repo rate rose to 18.31% at the daily tender from 17.35%, but the increase was well below market expectations. The repo rate reached a record 23.96% on Monday. The rate is the cost the South African Reserve Bank charges commercial banks to meet their daily borrowing requirements and is the most powerful mechanism for setting monetary policy. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Rand said he believes monetary policy is still the most appropriate approach in dealing with the soft rand, and that it's "unlikely" the government will change its fiscal policy to address the weak \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  But Peter Worthington, a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  analyst with J.P. Morgan in Johannesburg, said the government now needs to begin working on a revamp of its fiscal programs to lure offshore investors to South Africa. \par \par \uc2  Such a move would mirror the events of two years ago, when a sudden plunge by the rand in February 1996 brought a savage end to two years of stability and prodded the government to unveil its five-year Growth, Employment and Redistribution strategy, subsequently known as GEAR. The GEAR policy outlined a government commitment to bringing down the budget deficit, creating new jobs by encouraging investment, removing exchange controls and privatizing some state assets. \par \par \uc2  While the rand has almost consistently weakened since February 1996, many economists credit the government's actions in unveiling the GEAR strategy with slowing the rate of its descent. \par \par \uc2  The first three months of 1998 brought substantial overseas investment into South Africa's equity and bond markets, a relatively modest decline in the value of the rand and a substantial improvement in the Reserve Bank's gold and \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves. \par \par \uc2  But recent developments in Indonesia and Russia have soured investors' mood towards many emerging markets, precipitating renewed speculative attacks on the rand and heavy sales of South African bonds. \par \par \uc2  The depth of South Africa's social ills - crime, lack of housing and basic services and its young democracy - have marked it as an emerging economy. As such, there is still a high degree of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  risk. Investor confidence largely hinges upon the government's commitment to cutting its budget deficit and funding its massive social programs. \par \par \uc2  J.P. Morgan's Worthington believes the government needs to go further now to have the same impact it did in 1996. \par \par \uc2  "They need to issue a statement like GEAR and in it they should commit to accelerate privatization, take new steps to liberalize labor markets and do more to effectively tighten fiscal policy," he said. \par \par \uc2  But diagnosing and administering fresh fiscal medicine takes time, and Worthington said it is unlikely the government of President Nelson Mandela will announce any new action over the weekend or early next week. \par \par \uc2  Copyright (c) 1998 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. \par \par \uc2  All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2  1148 4214 \par \par \uc2 Dokument djon000020020329du6q00xlm\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
