\par\par \b \uc2  U.S. Fed  \highlight22\uc2 Intervenes \highlight\uc2 / \highlight22\uc2 South Africa \highlight\uc2  -4: Selling Dlrs For Rand \b0\par\par\uc2 236 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 Juni 1998\par 17:26\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  The Fed's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was conducted through traditional phone orders, not the Electronic Broking System, or EBS, traders said. \par \par \uc2  South Africa sought to exploit thinner trading volumes for rand in New York and London and the greater weight attached to the names of the U.S. and British central banks in the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , traders said. \par \par \uc2  However, the impact may prove limited when Johannesburg trading reopens Monday, traders said. The rand has already fallen 16% against the dollar this year and some said the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was only marginally more significant than a regular round of rand buying by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  in its local market. \par \par \uc2  It's significant that the neither the U.S. nor the U.K. is believed to have spent its own money. In general, if the U.S. spends its own money \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  it represents a change in policy, and the Treasury would comment accordingly, a step it hasn't taken. \par \par \uc2  The Reserve Bank spent $6.60 billion in May defending the rand, depleting its scant \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves. Thursday, the Reserve Bank dropped its key repo rate to 17.35%, however, setting off another wave of rand selling. \par \par \uc2  -By Paul Podolsky, Michael Casey, Charlene Lee, Carol Redmond, Damian Milverton and Andrea Chipman; 1-201-938-4384 \par \par \uc2  email: Paul.Podolsky@cor.dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones News