\par\par \b \uc2  FOCUS-S.AFRICA RESERVES DIP IN BATTLE FOR RAND. \b0\par\par\uc2 409 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 Dezember 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  JOHANNESBURG, Dec 1 (Reuters) - South Africa's gold and \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves dipped slightly to 26.5 billion rand in November from October's 27.3 billion, but economists said on Monday this masked hefty \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to defend the rand. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 South Africa\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said its use of foreign credit lines rose 1.1 billion rand to 9.9 billion by end November. \par \par \uc2  "Subtracting credit lines, the net reserves are worth around $3.4 billion, which is low by the standards of most countries. So the position of the reserves is still a concern," said UBS economist Costa Vayenas in London. \par \par \uc2  The data matched a Reuters consensus forecast carried out on November 28 which called for a fall to 26.5 billion rand. \par \par \uc2  It covered a month in which emerging markets around the world shuddered in a crisis of confidence as foreign investors ran for cover after Hong Kong stocks tumbled. \par \par \uc2  The rand plumbed fresh lows against the dollar and pound, and the stock and bond markets both suffered heavy losses in the fallout from the Asia epidemic. \par \par \uc2  But economists said that the rand could have fallen by more and speculated that it had been cushioned by heavy intevention by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  In the event it appeared that the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  had been significant, but probably not unduly substantial against the background of a massive run on emerging market assets. \par \par \uc2  "It's not really a bad number given the context of the current environment in world financial markets," said Equisec economist Dawie Roodt in Johannesburg. \par \par \uc2  But this gave no grounds for complacency. \par \par \uc2  "The position is not good. Our reserves are far from sufficient -- they only cover around 10 weeks worth of imports -- but are at least better than last year," he said. \par \par \uc2  South African import cover is now running at 2-1/2 months' worth compared with less than a month this time last year. \par \par \uc2  Standard Bank economists calculated that this cover was eroded to only eight weeks in November's financial turmoil, but did not think the position was life-threatening. \par \par \uc2  "South Africa's sound economic fundamental situation should ensure that the current account deficit is more than offset by net capital inflows in 1998, resulting in renewed build-up of foreign reserves," it said in a note to clients. \par \par \uc2  ((Alister Bull, Johannesburg newsroom, +27-11-482-1003 \par \par \uc2  newsroom@reuters.co.za)) \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020040131dtc100zvo\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
