\par\par \b \uc2  SAfrica c.bank reserves seen hit by  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2  By Justin McCamish \par \uc2 564 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 Oktober 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  JOHANNESBURG, Oct 29 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 South Africa\b0 \highlight\uc2 's Reserve Bank is estimated to have spent up to $1.5 billion defending the rand against speculators in the last few days of market turmoil, which saw the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  forced to all-time lows, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  But market participants were less certain of the damage the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's strategy of measured dollar selling to smooth rand fluctuation had wrought on its \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves. \par \par \uc2  Total \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves stood at 21.1 billion rand at the end of September. The Reserve Bank will release October figures on Monday. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the Bank was more active on Monday. \par \par \uc2  "At a rough guess they might have spent about $1.5 bln in two days but Tuesday might only have seen $100 million," said one Johannesburg \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  chief who declined to be named. \par \par \uc2  "Tuesday was a more organised depreciation (in the rand) because even though it was moving up, it seemed to a lot of us to follow the bonds. There was a lot of two-way business so not much need for the Bank to support it," said another dealer. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  investors were granted a respite on Wednesday as the rand stabilised around 4.81 to the dollar -- back from a 4.86/dollar record low plumbed on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  "I think you might see (the Bank) bleeding off some excess dollars from the market, and there are a few stale longs from London, but the Bank's not going to aggressively come in and buy now," one dealer said. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said the rand's six cent decline, coupled with a more than 200 percent rise in the money market shortage since Saturday, could not help but pare reserves. \par \par \uc2  But opinions were mixed as to where in the Bank's balance sheet -- forward \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  transactions, cash or utilisation of bank credit lines -- costs would be felt most. \par \par \uc2  "My own view is that they haven't dipped into the forward book. In other words, most of the liquidity given to the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  and money markets has come though spot reserves and possibly borrowed reserves," said Deutsche Morgan Grenfell economist Gordon Smith. \par \par \uc2  Another economist said: "They'll have done a combination (of spot and forward). They are trying to get their forward book down but if they needed to spend a lot then they would have made at least some use of that." \par \par \uc2  Others said the Bank might have stored additional dollars during the stability of early October, using them to soothe the rand's recent woes. \par \par \uc2  But economists said the Reserve Bank would generally be reluctant to deploy the forward book as it has been working hard to extract itself entirely from the expensive net oversold position it built over the first half of last year in defence of the rand, when the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  shed 20 percent against the dollar. \par \par \uc2  Economists and the International Monetary Fund have been urging the Bank to work faster on paring the forward books' oversold position -- revealed at $18 billion in August. \par \par \uc2  Some expressed concern that if the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  drags its heels, it could invite the kind of speculative attacks recently seen in Thailand, which has paid a high price for undermining its apparently ample reserves with forward trades. \par \par \uc2  -- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011003dtat03gy8\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
