\par\par \b \uc2  S. Africa Rand Falls On Fresh Dlr Surge, Local Bank Order \b0\par\par\uc2 225 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 September 1997\par 16:55\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  JOHANNESBURG (AP-Dow Jones)--South Africa's rand was driven lower Monday unable to withstand a surging dollar and a large order for the U.S. unit from two local banks. \par \par \uc2  Expectations of subdued trading ahead of Wednesday's Heritage Day national holiday, were dashed early in Monday's session as the dollar raced higher against the Deutsche mark and the yen. \par \par \uc2  The early dollar gains internationally barely registered on the rand initially. But a surprisingly large order for the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  by South Africa's Nedbank and Standard Bank - believed to be worth as much $100 million - broke key resistance levels, a dealer said. \par \par \uc2  London-based speculators joined the chase for dollars, yanking the unit above 4.7000 rand to an intraday high of 4.7140 rand - up almost four cents in little more than three hours. \par \par \uc2  Dealers reported midday \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \b \highlight22\uc2 South Africa\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to brake the rand selling spree. \par \par \uc2  'The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  wasn't all that emphatic, but with a few dollars flowing into a thin market it broke the dollar rally,' a dealer said. \par \par \uc2  Late Monday, the dollar was pegged at 4.6975 rand, up almost two-and-a-half cents from 4.6730 rand late Friday. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 22-09-97 \par \par \uc2  1455GMT \par \par \uc2  1059 1857 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt9m071zt\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
