\par\par \b \uc2  SAfrica Stals defends frx  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2 237 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 August 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  PRETORIA, Aug 26 (Reuter) - South African Reserve Bank Governor Chris Stals said on Tuesday that he disagreed with the International Monetary Fund's stance against \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. \par \par \uc2  "If we stop \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the markets today...interest rates will go up in \b \highlight22\uc2 South Africa\b0 \highlight\uc2  substantially, but because we \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market we try to keep interest rates at a reasonable level," he said. \par \par \uc2  In a statement released after a review of the South African economy the IMF argued that heavy purchases of the rand created confusion in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market and left the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  open to the risk of big trading losses. \par \par \uc2  The rand last week hit a record low against the U.S. dollar of 4.7910 bid, before bouncing back in part because of determined buying by the bank. \par \par \uc2  Stals rejected any suggestion that South Africa's interest rates were too low. \par \par \uc2  "We do our best to try and keep some kind of average, middle policy that will satisfy both international capital flows and domestic economic needs," he said. \par \par \uc2  The IMF board had advised South African authorities to tighten financial policies rather than \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market to protect the rand. \par \par \uc2  A few IMF directors even recommended that Pretoria increase interest rates should the rand face renewed heavy selling. \par \par \uc2  -- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011002dt8q00nm4\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
