\par\par \b \uc2  S. Africa/Repo/Amplifier -3: Stals Rejects IMF Stance \b0\par\par\uc2 247 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 August 1997\par 16:23\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  Stals' announcement, which came at the Reserve Bank's annual general meeting, caught onlookers off guard. \par \par \uc2  Market participants had hoped that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central-bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  chief would comment on monetary policy, but in the form of announcing a 1.0-percentage-point cut in the Bank rate to 16%, the first fall in four years. \par \par \uc2  In addition, the International Monetary Fund had only hours earlier declared in an annual review that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  should place less reliance on \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and more on monetary policy to react to exchange-rate movements. \par \par \uc2  Stals said growth in the broad money supply and private-sector credit extension remain too high for an easing of monetary policy. He also rejected the IMF's suggested approach to influencing the rand, saying interest rates would rise immediately were the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to abandon the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to market forces alone. \par \par \uc2  'We do our best to keep some kind of ... policy that will satisfy both international capital flows and domestic economic needs,' Stals told reporters. 'But the IMF has a very firm view on this: that we should not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the forward \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market or the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. Rather, we should let interest rates rise in \b \highlight22\uc2 South Africa\b0 \highlight\uc2  instead of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the markets. \par \par \uc2  'But if we stopped \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the markets today ... interest rates will go up in South Africa,' he added. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 26-08-97 \par \par \uc2  1423GMT \par \par \uc2  1193 4207 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt8q06a8m\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
