\par\par \b \uc2  S. Africa Rand/Dollar -2: Reserve Bank Not Seen In Market \b0\par\par\uc2 219 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 August 1997\par 10:52\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  JOHANNESBURG (AP-Dow Jones)--The dollar climbed to a record high of 4.7785 rand Thursday in a bout of speculative trading fueled by an absence of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \b \highlight22\uc2 South Africa\b0 \highlight\uc2 's Reserve Bank. \par \par \uc2  Around 0830 GMT, the dollar was quoted at 4.7745 rand, up more than three cents from 4.7420 rand late Wednesday. Minutes earlier it set a fresh peak of 4.7805 rand. \par \par \uc2  The dollar opened local trading hovering around 4.7500 rand, but with little resistance seen against further gains, the U.S. unit bolted higher quickly piercing its previous all-time high of 4.7690 rand set Oct. 31, 1996. \par \par \uc2  Dealers reported dollar buying from all quarters. 'Everybody is in buying - foreign banks and locals,' a dealer said. \par \par \uc2  'The way we are heading, it won't be long before we hit 4.8000 rand,' the dealer added. \par \par \uc2  Dealers reported no tangible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to brake the runaway dollar. \par \par \uc2  The dollar's record-setting pace is in sharp relief to its steady-to-lower performance against major European \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the yen early Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  The rand has lost 7.6% of its value against the dollar since April 4. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 21-08-97 \par \par \uc2  0852GMT \par \par \uc2  1059 1857 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt8l0669v\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
