\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 South Africa \highlight\uc2  Stals/Rates -3: Recent  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  "Small" \b0\par\par\uc2 216 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Juli 1997\par 18:37\par \uc2  Emerging Markets Report \par \uc2 EM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor, in London for a conference on southern Africa, said "it's going to be difficult" to hit the 10% money-supply annual growth target this quarter. \par \par \uc2  However, he added that the slowdown in gross domestic product growth earlier this year should help a decreasing money-supply growth rate follow. \par \par \uc2  Looking at the recent speculative pressure on South Africa's rand, Stals insisted that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was ready to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  more if necessary to support the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The Reserve Bank sold dollars for rand late Wednesday, with Stals describing the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  as "relatively small." \par \par \uc2  He said the market's nervousness about falling gold prices and their potential impact on the rand has been exaggerated. \par \par \uc2  "This is much more about perception," he said, adding that the speculation is "nothing comparable to last year." \par \par \uc2  The rand came under speculative attack in 1996, falling 22% against the dollar. Late Thursday in Johannesburg, the dollar was pegged at 4.5505 rand, off more than a cent from 4.5615 rand late Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Stals said rather than the exchange rate, falling gold prices are a concern for South African employment levels, which now stand above 30%. \par \par \uc2  (END) DOW JONES EMERGING MARKETS REPORT 10-07-97 \par \par \uc2  1637GMT \par \par \uc2  1802 1803 1896 \par \par \uc2 Dokument em00000020011006dt7a0082w\par }\pa