\par\par \b \uc2  S. Africa Rand Gains Solidly; Dealers Smell  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 225 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 Dezember 1996\par 15:17\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1996, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  JOHANNESBURG (AP-Dow Jones)--\b \highlight22\uc2 South Africa\b0 \highlight\uc2 's rand gained solidly against most major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  Thursday, with dealers citing another buying foray by the South African Reserve Bank. \par \par \uc2  Unnamed \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  officials were quoted in local newspapers Thursday as saying reports of their \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market were exaggerated, but dealers remain adamant the rand's recent strength is entirely attributable to buying from the Reserve Bank. \par \par \uc2  Late Thursday, the dollar was quoted at 4.6655 rand, down from 4.6835 rand Wednesday. The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has dropped nine South African cents against the rand since the Reserve Bank was seen selling dollars around 4.7555 rand late last Thursday. \par \par \uc2  'The (Reserve Bank) is trying to tell us that the dollar is going to lose six cents like it did Wednesday on exporter selling? I don't think so,' remarked one dealer at a major local bank. \par \par \uc2  'I think we saw one small exporter in the market today and yet the dollar's down another two cents. The (rand) buying is definitely coming from Pretoria,' he said. \par \par \uc2  The dollar meandered through the first half of the session within a 4.6800-4.6900 rand band before dropping a cent-and-a-half within an hour. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 19-12-96 \par \par \uc2  1417GMT \par \par \uc2  1059 1857 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011014dscj01tlj\par }\page {\par\fs20{\