\par\par \b \uc2  S. Africa's  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\uc2 /Rand -3: Stals To Speak Tuesday \b0\par\par\uc2 243 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 Februar 1996\par 08:58\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1996, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  The dealer said trading in the rand so far Tuesday has been dominated by local market participants with very little action seen from overseas-based customers. \par \par \uc2  'We saw offshore clients taking the lead Friday but today they're quiet and the rand should stabilize around current levels,' the dealer said. \par \par \uc2  He sees the rand oscillating within a 3.8300-3.8900 rand trading band during the remainder of dealings Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Panic selling wiped 3.4% from the value of the rand against the dollar Friday as investors reacted to speculation that exchange controls on residents could be relaxed within weeks, reports that President Nelson Mandela was unwell and a bearish rand report by Union Bank of Switzerland. \par \par \uc2  Selling pressure was maintained Monday, driving the South African \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to a record low of 3.8900 rand against the dollar before recovering thanks to \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Chris Liebenberg, \b \highlight22\uc2 South Africa\b0 \highlight\uc2 's minister of finance, told a business gathering Tuesday the rand's sudden weakness won't deter the government from continuing with its policy of eventually removing exchange controls. \par \par \uc2  Liebenberg also warned that South Africa 'will not use our foreign reserves to flood the market' in support of a weakening rand. \par \par \uc2  Chris Stals, the Reserve Bank Governor, is scheduled to deliver an address to a business gathering in Johannesburg around 0900 GMT Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 20-02-96 \par \par \uc2  0758GMT 