\par\par \b \uc2  Rand crashes in Europe, hits all time low. \b0\par\par\uc2 412 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 Februar 1996\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1996 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, Feb 16 (Reuter) - The South African rand was sold in Europe, with continued liquidation forcing it down to a new all time low versus the dollar. \par \par \uc2  Funds out of Europe and some in the U.S. were looking for reasons to sell and rumours that exchange controls were about to be lifted, although denied, hit the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  At 1220 GMT the rand was quoted at 3.80/81 per dollar -- a massive spread compared with the usual 20 or 25 ticks -- more than four percent down from Thursday's high. The old all time low of 3.7155 was set on July 26, 1994. \par \par \uc2  "These are the excuses people are using but the bottom line is that it's been a great yield play," said one trader. \par \par \uc2  "The whole market was all round the same way playing the yield, and bang," he said. "Everyone was short dollars, there was only one way it could go." \par \par \uc2  Traders said because the rand had been steady for so long a major imbalance had built up with exporters hedging their dollar receipts forward to take advantage of the yield while the importers were happy to hold off and do nothing. \par \par \uc2  "The market appears to have got itself heavily oversold having been taking the yield on the stable rand ever since the abolition of the financial rand," said Macer Gifford, exotic \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  specialist at Standard Chartered in London. \par \par \uc2  South African Finance Minister Chris Liebenberg denied a relaxation of exchange controls was imminent and the finance ministry said earlier that there had been no change in the plan to phase the lifting of restrictions. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said it is now up to the Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 South Africa\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  and restore some order to the market and there has been talk of covert \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  buying on the open market this morning. \par \par \uc2  In a research paper published earlier this week UBS said the rand was seven to 10 percent overvalued versus the dollar. \par \par \uc2  "According to our purchasing power parity estimates, the rand is now some 7-10 percent overvalued against the U.S. dollar," the paper said. \par \par \uc2  "With the current account balance set to worsen the rand's current trading range can only be sustained if measures are adopted to reduce overheating pressures in the economy and to cut the growing current account deficit," it said. \par \par \uc2  -- Phil Smith, London Newsroom, +44-71-510-6284. \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1996 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011019ds2g01esx\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
