\par\par \b \uc2  S.Africa's Stals opposes undue rand gain right now. \b0\par\par\uc2 404 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 Februar 1995\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1995 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  JOHANNESBURG, Feb 20 (Reuter) - \b \highlight22\uc2 South Africa\b0 \highlight\uc2 's Reserve (\b \highlight22\uc2 central) Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will continue to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to prevent an undue appreciation of the rand at this stage, the Bank's governor Chris Stals said. \par \par \uc2  "In the current situation and pending certain exchange control relaxations, the Reserve Bank will continue to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market in order to prevent an undue appreciation of the rand at this stage," he said in a statement announcing a tightening of monetary policy. \par \par \uc2  Within the framework of existing exchange controls on capital outflows, any excessive inflow of foreign capital could, at least before exchange controls are relaxed, exert pressures for an appreciation of the exchange rate, he said. \par \par \uc2  To relieve these, the Bank must \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  regularly in the market to absorb the surplus \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  and to prevent a rand appreciation which would, at this stage, contribute further to the erosion of South Africa's competitive position in international markets. \par \par \uc2  It was an illusion to believe South Africa could be made more competitive merely by devaluing the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , he said. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prevent any undue rand appreciation did however create prime liquidity and, if not counteracted or sterilised, added to the ability of banking institutions to provide more credit to their clients, he said. \par \par \uc2  Over the past seven months, the Reserve Bank's net foreign reserves rose 6.8 billion rand, resulting in a similar amount of liquidity being created by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  This conflict of objectives, to raise foreign reserves and prevent an undue rand appreciation on the one hand, and on the other to keep money supply under control, required the use of more than just discount rate as a monetary policy instrument. \par \par \uc2  Hence the announced tightening of banks' minimum reserve requirements as part of a new package to tighten monetary policy, including a rise in discount rate to 14 from 13 percent. \par \par \uc2  He said there was a "dire" need for the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to raise its foreign reserves to a more acceptable level. Their present value at 11.3 billion rand was barely enough to cover six weeks' imports and should be raised to a level of at least three months' imports, he said. \par \par \uc2  The bank therefore used every opportunity to obtain surplus foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  from the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to supplement its reserves, he added. \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1995 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011104dr2k012kg\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
